  "question": {
    "text": "Number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>-digit numbers (the repetition of digits is allowed) which are made using the digits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> , and are divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> , is equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "21",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>We have to form four-digit number using the digits&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Now for number to be divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math>&nbsp;we need to fix the last digit as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;as&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>_</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>, so that number can be divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and for divisibility by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;the addition of all number should be divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>,</p><p>So making cases where sum is divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p>Case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mtext>as&#160;</mtext><mn>1</mn><mo>,1,2&#160;&#38;&#160;5</mo><mtext>&#160;sum&#160;is&#160;divisible&#160;by&#160;</mtext><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So, total ways&nbsp;for case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;ways,</p><p>Case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ways</mtext><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ways</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><mtext>&#160;ways</mtext></math></p><p>So, total ways for case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;ways.</p><p>Case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>6</mn><mtext>&#160;ways</mtext></math></p><p>Case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ways</mtext></math></p><p>So, adding all cases we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math>&nbsp;ways.</p>"
  }
}